@tr1v3r/dsh-proxy README · How it works：DSH and pi-ai issue requests through `globalThis.fetch`, which reads undici's
well-known global dispatcher slot (`Symbol.for('undici.globalDispatcher.1')`).
The plugin owns that slot:

@tr1v3r/dsh-proxy README · Applied route snapshot：The General settings row can read the host's **last applied default route**
through an optional, authenticated Connection Fetch route. It shows the selected mode,
source, separately redacted HTTP/HTTPS endpoints, bypass policy, generation and
stable apply/fallback code. Refresh explicitly after a save if the host has not
applied that revision yet. Unsupported/disconnected hosts show “unavailable”;
normal settings and quick switching still work without this capability.

@tr1v3r/dsh-proxy README · What is covered / not covered：Also note: child processes already running when you flip the switch keep the
env they were spawned with; undici's SOCKS5 agent is currently marked
experimental upstream.
